Implement user story SKY-004-be-1: Build Express REST API server with /health, /search, /cheapest, and static dashboard — Implementation

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts — an Express HTTP server exposing GET /health, GET /search, GET /cheapest, and GET / (static dashboard from src/public/index.html read at runtime). Export named `app` separately from guarded `listen()`. RAPIDAPI_KEY absence gates /search and /cheapest with 503 but not /health or /. SkyscannerClient errors return 500 without crashing. FlightResult type imported from SKY-002. Update package.json with 'start' and 'build' scripts; build must copy src/public/ to dist/public/. Add supertest and @types/supertest to devDependencies. Depends on SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports a named `app` (Express instance) separately from the `listen()` call; `listen()` is guarded by main-module check (`import.meta.url === pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href` for ESM or `require.main === module` for CJS) matching the tsup output format so `vitest run` never binds a port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 JSON { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence; /health is never gated
- GET / returns HTTP 200 text/html with body equal to contents of src/public/index.html read at runtime via fs.readFileSync (not hardcoded inline HTML); not gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET /search: valid params (from, to, date, adults) → 200 { flights: FlightResult[], count, searchedAt: ISO-8601 } where count === flights.length and searchedAt is distinct per request; missing required param (from/to/date) → 400 { error }; adults absent → defaults to 1; adults non-numeric → 400 { error }
- GET /cheapest: valid params (from, to, date) → 200 with single cheapest FlightResult (price ≤ all others); empty results → 404 { error }; missing required param → 400 { error }; adults defaults to 1 if absent
- RAPIDAPI_KEY absent at startup → middleware short-circuits /search and /cheapest with 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / unaffected
- SkyscannerClient throws error → server returns 500 { error } without crash or unhandled promise rejection; FlightResult type imported from SKY-002 export (not redeclared inline)
- package.json has 'start': 'node dist/server.js'; 'build' script produces dist/server.js and copies src/public/ to dist/public/ so GET / serves the real file after build; supertest and @types/supertest in devDependencies





